  jokes:
  - innerList:
    - The cow comedian? udderly amoosing.
    - Wha's a no legged cow? ground beef
    - What's a one legged cow? steak
    - What's a two legged cow? lean beef
    - What's a three legged cow? a tri tip
    - What's a four legged cow?
    - What's a five legged cow? a bull
    - What's a seven legged cow? tri tip
    - "In the Firste Morrow, Yunhu arriveth at the Abbey of the Laughing Heifers
      Wherein dwelleth monks of the Order of the Wry Moo, clad in robes of cowhide
      stitched with quips profound. There stood the elder, Pungurus the Hilarious,
      who spake thus:  \u201CHark, O Yunhu, seeker of wit most rare, here is a jest
      to quicken thy heart and lighten thy soul:  Why doth the kine cross the yonder
      road?  To reach the greener pastures anon, methinks\u2014nay, to escape the
      pestilent knave, Sir Farmer\u2019s scythe!*  But Yunhu, with furrowed brow
      and visage stern, replied, \u201CMethinks thy jest lacketh the apex of mirth.
      Pray, grant me the True Jest, lest I falter in mine holy quest!\u201D  Upon
      the Second Dawn, he ventured to the Valley of the Udder Wherein ancient bovines
      whispered secrets in tongue of moo and low. There, the Oracle Bovina bestowed
      upon him a riddle wrapped in riddle, cloaked in whimsy:  \"What saith the cow
      in reverie deep?\"  Yunhu pondered, \u201CMayhap \u2018Moo,\u2019 or perchance
      \u2018Methinks I am a dragon in disguise\u2019?\u201D  The Oracle chuckled,
      \u201CNay, the answer lies within thine own heart: \u2019Moo-ve along, mortal,
      lest I trample thy folly!\u2019\u201D  At the Final Eve, atop the Hill of Jestful
      Reckoning Yunhu, weary and bedeviled by puns uncountable, sat \u2018neath the
      Great Oak of Jest and spake thus:  \u201CAlas, hath I wandered far and wide
      through dale and fen, seeking but a humble cow joke to sate mine hunger for
      laughter.\u201D  Then, lo and behold, a humble calf did approach and utter
      thus:  \"Why doth the cow not wear a bell?  Because her horns do ring louder
      than any tinkling knell!\u201D  In that moment, the heavens didst part, the
      stars twinkled in syncopation, and Yunhu burst forth in laughter most hearty,
      for the jest was at once both simple and sublime\u2014the very essence of mirth! 
      Thus, good folk, learn from the tale of Yunhu: the best cow joke need not be
      a labyrinthine riddle, but oft the simplest \u201CMoo\u201D mayst bring the
      greatest joy."
    - Moove out of the way!
    - Yunhu was playing an online multiplayer farmers vs alien game. Despite being
      being at losing positing in his own game, he deleted the opponent's player
      prefab in the hierarchy. It was a cowculated move.
    - Guess what? cow butt
    - cow thihphgsfpi ok yeah
  - innerList:
    - A snake with a great personality? snake charmer
    - boutta get my hiss-preso
    - 'FUN FACT: snakes love boa-ling'
    - hissterical
    - snake you later!
    - snakes don't have legs. so we point and laugh.
    - snakes don't have arms. so we point and laugh.
    - snakes have tails so we points and laugh
    - did you know that the snake can jump higher than a eiffel tower? thats because
      eiffel tower no jumpy
  - innerList:
    - walrous
    - walrous are kinda fat
    - tusk you later!
    - among us
    - im sending you to tuskany
    - walruses are dumb
    - bubber you later!
  jokeText: {fileID: 1250228397}
